TI  - Prediction of Future Health Care Utilization.
PG  - 1090-1091
LID - 10.3233/SHTI220282 [doi]
AB  - Psychosocial factors are known to have adverse health impacts, but are rarely 
      measured; using natural language processing, we extracted factors that identified 
      a higher risk segment of older adults with multimorbidity. We find these 
      extracted features are highly predictive of future emergency department visits 
      and hospitalizations, although only marginal prediction gains are seen compared 
      to other models without these factors. Combining these extraction techniques with 
      other measures of social determinants may help catalyze population health efforts 
      to mitigate these health impacts.
