VI  - 2020
DP  - 2020
TI  - Identification of Gout Flares in Chief Complaint Text Using Natural Language 
      Processing.
PG  - 973-982
AB  - Many patients with gout flares treated in the Emergency Department (ED) often do 
      not receive optimal continuity of care after an ED visit. Thus, developing 
      methods to identify patients with gout flares in the ED and referring them to 
      appropriate outpatient gout care is required. While Natural Language Processing 
      (NLP) has been used to detect gout flares retrospectively, it is much more 
      challenging to identify patients prospectively during an ED visit where 
      documentation is usually minimal. We annotate a corpus of ED triage nurse chief 
      complaint notes for the presence of gout flares and implement a simple algorithm 
      for gout flare ED alerts. We show that the chief complaint alone has strong 
      predictive power for gout flares. We make available a de-identified version of 
      this corpus annotated for gout mentions, which is to our knowledge the first free 
      text chief complaint clinical corpus available.
